1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,420
We've all been there:

2
00:00:01,440 --> 00:00:03,820
"Oh no, we need to go to emergency!"

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,540
Public or private, the first thing that happens

4
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:07,820
is triage.

5
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,620
A nurse checks how sick you are,

6
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:12,060
and everyone is sorted by urgency.

7
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,180
The sickest are seen first.

8
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,060
Arriving by ambulance doesn't get you seen sooner.

9
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:19,100
You're triaged the same way as someone who

10
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,060
walked in.

11
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:22,620
That's where ambulance ramping comes from.

12
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:25,300
Paramedics must stay with their patient until the

13
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,207
emergency team can take over.

14
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:30,060
When it's full, ambulances wait outside.

15
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,540
That's ramping.

16
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,460
Public emergency departments see a lot more people.

17
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:35,687
Depending on the day,

18
00:00:35,707 --> 00:00:37,500
the time, and what's going on,

19
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:39,500
you could be there for hours.

20
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,940
Arrive at 5pm, and you might not leave

21
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:43,500
until the early hours.

22
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:45,820
Some staff even swear a full moon makes

23
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:47,073
it busier!

24
00:00:47,093 --> 00:00:50,273
Private emergency departments usually have fewer people.

25
00:00:50,293 --> 00:00:52,700
Often you're triaged, and treatment has started within

26
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,993
about an hour, depending on the day.

27
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,673
But you will pay.

28
00:00:56,693 --> 00:00:58,860
Until you're admitted, it's like seeing a private

29
00:00:58,880 --> 00:00:59,847
specialist.

30
00:00:59,867 --> 00:01:02,180
Your health fund usually only starts paying once

31
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,860
you're admitted, just like planned surgery.

32
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:06,620
The fee depends on the hospital,

33
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:08,353
often a few hundred dollars,

34
00:01:08,373 --> 00:01:10,087
sometimes four or five hundred.

35
00:01:10,107 --> 00:01:12,620
Tests and scans may be billed separately.

36
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:15,260
Many private emergency departments will tell you after

37
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:17,527
triage if you're likely to be admitted,

38
00:01:17,547 --> 00:01:18,780
before you're charged.

39
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,087
Then the doctor sees you,

40
00:01:20,107 --> 00:01:22,167
and you have any tests or scans.

41
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:24,407
If you're admitted, your fund kicks in.

42
00:01:24,427 --> 00:01:25,420
You pay your excess,

43
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:27,953
and sign paperwork showing any gaps.

44
00:01:27,973 --> 00:01:29,900
There's often no gap for the doctors,

45
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:31,580
but it will be in writing.

46
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:33,820
On many policies, if you've already paid your

47
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:36,460
excess this year, you don't pay it again.

48
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:38,300
Some funds count the calendar year,

49
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:39,660
some the financial year,

50
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,020
so check yours.

51
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:43,553
From there, your fund helps cover the hospital,

52
00:01:43,573 --> 00:01:45,340
the operating theatre and more,

53
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:46,940
just like planned surgery.

54
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:48,540
That's your safety net.

55
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:50,700
Can you go to a private emergency department

56
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:51,900
without insurance?

57
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:54,060
Yes, you'll pay the same visit fee.

58
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:55,527
But if you're admitted,

59
00:01:55,547 --> 00:01:57,980
expect to pay a large deposit up front,

60
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,060
because a stay in intensive care can cost

61
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:01,980
tens of thousands of dollars.

62
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,820
So why not skip insurance,

63
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,820
save your money, and just pay for surgery

64
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,420
yourself if you ever need it?

65
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:08,940
There are catches.

66
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:10,740
That's our next video!
